  "reversal_definition": "A row whose predicted ordering of the analysed heads disagrees with their measured ordering: Kendall tau (tau-a over the three head pairs, concordant minus discordant over 3) below zero, with no tied pair on either side. The tau is taken per row across heads - it says nothing about how the heads rank rows.",
  "tie_policy": "A pair whose two measured labels are equal has no ordering to reverse, and tau is deflated rather than negative on such a row, so a row with a tied pair (on either side) is counted under `tied_rows` and left out of `reversal_rows`. `tau_negative_rows` counts every negative tau, so the difference between the two is visible rather than silent.",
  "selection_pool": "forbidden",
  "selection_pool_note": "Head-order reversal is a reported result and not a case-selection pool (#129 AC9). Requiring every inverted pair to clear the replicate noise floor leaves a single row, so lowering the margin to fill a pool would report measurement noise as model failure. Case selection uses cross-head error disagreement instead, from predictions and labels alone. This report therefore carries counts and distributions, and no list of rows to pick from.",
